# Rover Twelve (Clegg), 1912-1924.
#
# Owen Clegg's 2,297 cc side-valve four, 75 x 130 mm, 22-28 bhp, three-speed
# gearbox. 4,140-4,267 mm long, 1,651 mm wide, 2,794-2,946 mm wheelbase,
# 1,270 mm track, 711 kg chassis. About 5,000 were built before 1914 and about
# 13,000 in total; the model was renamed Rover 14 for 1924.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_12
# https://collection.powerhouse.com.au/object/206829
#
# Colours: Black, Dark Green, Maroon and Grey, as specified for this model.
#
# Weight: 13 in total (black 5, green 4, maroon 2, grey 2). Classes 2,3 and a
# low-volume prestige car, so the total stays inside the 10-15 band.
#
# Speed 70 km/h (45 mph), the Powerhouse Museum figure for its 1912 tourer;
# Rover itself claimed 75 km/h.
# Comfort 60/420 (line). Classes 2,3.
# Dates: 1912-1924 with a road tail to about 1949.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-twelve.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rover-twelve/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.
#
# Photographs: all four are open tourers.
# rover12-a.jpg 1911 12 hp four-seater side view, public domain,
# https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1911_Rover_12hp_4-seater_torpedo.jpg
# rover12-b.jpg 1912 tourer front three-quarter, CC BY 2.0, David Maciulaitis,
# https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1912_Rover_12_(15862397462).jpg
# rover12-c.jpg 1914 tourer front three-quarter, CC BY-SA 2.0, Clive Barker,
# https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1914_Rover_12_tourer_(14952757061).jpg
# rover12-d.jpg 1923 Clegg tourer front three-quarter, CC BY 2.0, Steve Glover,
# https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1923_Rover_12_Clegg.jpg

